      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a95256f54d514123c1f089d|full_name}: Yep I mentioned how the orange functionality is the same as green with hidden location.\nMy feature request it to provide the choices and control for many scenarios and being blue while hiding your location is no different to how it works now. Functionally you might think its stupid but it already works to stop everyone joining you by seeing youre in a private world. Its a scenario that provides more privacy but encourages friends to join that still want to or know that it wont be a bother.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-02-27T04:21:31.202Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Forcing the Orange status to hide your information is not ideal in every situation.\nI suggest keeping the four status colours and how they handle invites is perfect. The change involves separating the ability to hide world information. Essentially add a toggle for users to hide their world information instead of automatically forcing it.\nFor example this would allow the ability for the Ask Me orange status to force all joiners to ask for an invite while still allowing people to see if you are in private or not. Extending the situations that the Orange status can be used for.\nFor  the Green, Blue and Orange status it may be useful to still display if you are in a public instance as this helps friends know that you are more likely to accept. On the flip side it can be handy to hide information but let the status indicate to friends what you prefer they do.\nRed can remain as is. These changes would benefit Orange the most but be useful for Green and Blue.",
